review:
It's a shame that so many new people rate this game bad just because they were to lazy to read the store description or at least the product title besides of the buy button. They would notice that they buy the first episode for a few cents.

It's the best RE title besides the classics in my opinion. The whole gameplay feels more like a classic title than 4,5,6 together.

Great storytelling especially Barry's and Natalia's part; 
Some nostaglia values;
Good "puzzles"; 
No parasites;
A virus; 
Mutant bosses;
Well-made connection to the RE storyline; 
Over 130h of gameplay if you want to unlock all the ingame items; 
Additional residentevil.net challenges;
Good AI for singleplayers - It always did what i wanted during my 125 hours of gameplay; 
No QTEs as present in RE5 or RE6; (There is a huge difference between an QTE and an prompt, a really huge difference)
Good graphics and performance;
Great controls - better than in the previous OTS titles; (go and adjust you hardware, like sensitivity, acceleration etc.)
Most improved bonus mode, RAID,  (4th survivour, merchs, raid... they all share the same idea)
Well-made DLC modes.

[b][MAY CONTAIN SOME MINOR SPOILERS - READ AT YOUR OWN RISK][/b]

[b]Resident Evil: Revelations 2[/b] isn't a direct continuation form the first [i]Revelations[/i] game as one might think from reading the name, it does happen after and there are a few mentions about things that happened during the first game, but that's all.
The story is good, despite the fact that I don't enjoy this chapter thing, on this game it was interesting, because the end of each chapter made us super curious to see what was going to happen next.
Just like in the first game, it brings back two original characters, [b]Barry[/b] from [i]Resident Evil 1[/i] and [b]Claire[/b] from [i]Resident Evil 2[/i] and [i]Resident Evil: Code Veronica[/i], it also brought two new characters to assist them, [b]Moira[/b], Barry's daughter and [b]Natalia[/b], a young girl who is a survivor of the Terragrigia Panic (an event that happened pior to the events from Resident Evil: Revelations and is shown during that game).
The Raid Mode is back and is sure to give several hours of fun.

There are some performance issues on both the normal game and raid mode, things such as FPS drop and stuttering, on both good and bad PCs and with any graphics settings, some people reported issues with data upload on raid mode, but nothing of that happened to me, so I cannot say for sure if it's going on or not.
Capcom is slowly fixing them and the game is way better now than it was on release, but it's still far from perfect.

[b]Pros and Cons:[/b]

[b]Pros:[/b]
• Original characters from first games;
• Interesting and fun character mechanics;
• Excelent story;
• Overall graphics quality is good;
• Game can be very hard or very easy to suit your play style;
• Good controls (Xbox 360 Controller is highly recommended);
• Replay value, you can play the game to unlock things;
• Raid mode is awesome, fun and nearly infinte;
• RE.Net support for online events, items and records tracking.

[b]Cons:[/b]
• FPS drops (especially near world light sources or near fog and particles) even on PCs that are very superior to the game recommended specs;
• The AI is dumb, you should not wait for them to get away from enemies or they'll make you waste lots of healing items, it's better if you simply switch to them and run away from threats;
• The game is divided in chapters (not a big deal now that all of them are already released);
• Some unnecessary expensive DLC and in-game transactions for weapons, upgrades and "continues".


[b]Conclusion: [/b]

I really enjoyed the game, the good parts are worth over the bad parts (mostly the performance issues which as I said, are slowly being fixed).
It is worth the money and the game should give you some quality playtime for some good time.
